*.swp
*.DS_Store
**/__pycache__/**
*.egg-info
# Anchored: setuptools writes a full second copy of the package into build/
# when a wheel or sdist is built, and an unanchored rule would also hide
# proteusfold/'s own build output, which its nested .gitignore already covers.
/build/
/dist/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.idea/*
.vscode/
**/.ipynb_checkpoints/**
/output/
/wandb/
# Anchored: an unanchored `data/` also matches any nested directory called
# `data`, which is how a leaked path in a vendored config once escaped a
# repo-wide grep (the search honoured this file).
/data/
examples/data/
/.venv/
# uv.lock is deliberately NOT ignored: it is what makes `uv sync` reproducible.
*.pth
# Editable figure sources. Figure1.ai is a 4.35 MB PDF-compatible Illustrator
# file whose XMP metadata carries the author's local Windows path; the rendered
# docs/img/*.png is what the README shows and what ships.
*.ai
*pkl
nohup.out
*.log
